cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it was written for."
title: "luhdm: levitated-sensor ultraheavy dark matter analysis and v10 data release"
abstract: >-
  Physics models and limit setting for the search for ultraheavy dark matter
  with a magnetically levitated particle: halo and atmospheric propagation, the
  straight-line-impulse cross section, the bridge to the optimum_interval
  statistics package, and the scripts and notebooks that build the data release
  and the figures in the paper.
type: software
version: "10.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Concept DOI of the Zenodo deposit: resolves to the latest version, which is
# what a citation should point at. The version DOI of v10 is 10.5281/zenodo.22018170.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22018169
keywords:
  - dark matter
  - ultraheavy dark matter
  - levitated sensor
  - optimum interval
  - direct detection
repository-code: "https://github.com/PolonaiseExperiment/luhdm"
